# Generic asset and portrait routing patch template

Apply to the live repository's existing asset skill after discovering its actual name and ownership model.

## Required source-mode rule

Grounded real people use attributed real source photographs or user-authorized source photographs. Never generate a substitute person. Preserve the immutable source, exact crop, crop coordinates, crop equality evidence, provenance, rights notes, subject-ownership disposition, and checksums.

## Required handoff split

The sourced-asset role owns source research and exact crop evidence, then stops.

The `hoi4-portrait-pipeline` skill and `hoi4_portrait_pipeline` subagent own deterministic preparation, conditional colorization, restoration, masks, approved background replacement, Krea 2 identity-edit candidates, HOI4 style LoRA use, comparisons, manifests, and final PNG/DDS only after a separate audit PASS.

The `hoi4_portrait_identity_auditor` is read-only. It reviews randomized candidates, cannot see producer ranking, and returns schema-valid identity, style, mask, and provenance verdicts. It cannot generate, edit, rank, select, resize, or convert candidates.

The parent repository agent chooses among independently eligible candidates, copies the accepted DDS to the correct runtime path, wires the character and GFX references, validates a live in-game consumer, and owns the completion claim.

## Required fail-closed language

A candidate with any mandatory FAIL or UNCERTAIN audit gate is ineligible. Style quality never compensates for identity drift. Missing source, crop, provenance, threshold calibration, background, model, node, workflow, audit, or DDS evidence blocks completion.

## Required real-person sequence

Attributed immutable photograph -> exact head-and-shoulders crop with equality evidence -> source-locked Krea 2 production through `hoi4-portrait-pipeline` -> deterministic 156x210 processing -> independent audit by a separate process -> validated DDS -> parent-owned runtime wiring and live-consumer proof.
